+**Daytona Championship USA** (Sega Amusements, 2017; New Season Edition 2019,
+`Sega/Daytona/Daytona.exe` v190306, 32-bit, Direct3D 11, fixed base, no symbols):
+
+- **Shell protocol (`WAL_SEGASHELL_PROTOCOL=dyt`).** Magic `DYT`, one numbering both ways (names
+  at `0x1543be0`, `0x584970`): game 0x00-0x2b (keepalive, launched, assets loaded, attract,
+  start pressed, mode / track / car / transmission select, race events, game over, high
+  scores, 0x2a security challenge, 0x2b shutdown), Shell 0x2c `SET_SKU` (data byte 1), 0x2d
+  `SETCREDIT`, 0x2e `SECURITY_AUTHENTICATE`, 0x2f `RESET`, 0x30 `EXIT`, 0x31-0x33 party mode
+  (handlers: the jump table at `0x5845c8`). The payload answers `LAUNCHED_OK` with `SET_SKU`
+  and the credits. The game sends a 4-byte challenge every 10 seconds and quits after 5
+  unanswered (`0x584d09`): patched to never quit (`0x584d0f` `jle` -> `jmp`).
+- **I/O board.** A DirectInput game controller "SEGA IO Controller" (the first `DIJOYSTATE`, axes
+  -1000..1000, `0x47cdf0`): X the wheel (calibrated by `ShellData.ini` `[CalibrationData]`), Z
+  the brake, Rx the gas; its buttons map to game functions through the table of known
+  controllers at `0x116d490` (0xe0 per device: name, then 12 (button, function) pairs): 0 start
+  (function 2), 1 / 2 / 6 / 7 functions 7-10, 3 / 4 functions 14 / 13, 8-11 functions 3-6
+  (likely the view buttons, shift and gears 1-4; not verified: no camera change seen). Menus: the wheel chooses, the
+  gas pedal or start selects. Credits come from the Shell (`SETCREDIT`), free play from
+  `ShellData.ini` `[Credit] Freeplay`. Its Shell and data paths are already relative
+  (`../shell/Game.ini`, `../ShellData`, `../GameData`).
+- **Force feedback (`inpwrapper.rs`, `WAL_SEGASHELL_INPWRAPPER=1`).** The game starts the Shell's
+  64-bit `c:\sega\shell\InpWrapper.exe -h=<game window> -p=<port>` (`0x5283e0`, `Game.ini`
+  `ParallelPort`=888), which registers its window (`WM_COPYDATA` `dwData` 3) and then gets each
+  force byte (`SendMessageTimeoutA` `WM_COPYDATA` `dwData` 0x20, `0x528de0`) for
+  `inpoutx64.dll`'s `Out32`. The payload answers the `CreateProcessA`, registers a made-up window
+  and takes the game's sends to it: the byte (`0x528ef0`: low nibble 1 strongest .. 15 weakest,
+  0 none, bit 0x10 a force to the right) goes to `port_ffb` (`WAL_SEGASHELL_FFB_FORMAT=daytona`,
+  SEGA Rally 3's decoding on port 0x378): `output::FFB_CONSTANT`.
+- Boot: about 2 minutes to attract on a new prefix ("Data Loading ... %" while its shaders
+  compile), about 30 seconds once the shader caches are warm.
